    "summary": "Spear gun (linti) (for fishing) made of wood, plastic, rubber. The stock is made of wood and has a barrel made out of a bic yellow biro which has been cut to shape, this is attched with red rubber (probably cut from a bicycle inner tube). Spear (for fishing) made of metal (attached to 39a). The spear is very thin and designed to be shot through the bic biro barrel of 39a. The spear has been knotched at the butt end to allow the attachment of a rubber band.",
